    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "pf_14355b59_value",
      "label": "Paragraph4 — Value",
      "default": "Your Mane Master™ is lovingly made with natural wood, painted details, and premium bristles — so it deserves a little TLC to keep it looking (and working) its best. Here’s how to keep it clean and happy:<br>\n<br>1. After each use, gently remove any trapped hair with your fingers or a wide-tooth comb to prevent build-up.\n<br><br>2. Mix a small amount of gentle shampoo or mild soap with lukewarm water — but avoid soaking the whole brush, as water and wood don’t mix well!\n<br><br>3. Dip a clean toothbrush or soft cloth into the soapy water and softly scrub the bristles and base. Be careful not to saturate the wooden handle or painted areas.<br><br>4. Wipe the brush with a clean, damp cloth to remove any soap residue. Then, dry the bristles with a towel and lay the brush bristle-side down to air dry completely.<br><br><strong>Important:</strong> Never submerge your Mane Master™ in water — this can damage the wood and paint over time.\n<br><br><strong>Top Tip:</strong> Give your Mane Master™ a gentle clean every 1–2 weeks for the smoothest, healthiest hair experience!<br> "
    },
